<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prabu Geusan Ulun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prabu Geusan Ulun was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumedang">Sumedang</a> Larang in the Priangan highlands of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in the late 16th century. After the Banten Sultanate destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakuan-pajajaran">Pakuan Pajajaran</a> in 1579, he received the Sundanese royal regalia, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binokasih">Binokasih crown</a>, and claimed to rule as heir of the Sunda Kingdom over much of the Priangan. Sumedang's museum of regalia is named after him.</p></div>
